linode:index/databaseAccessControls:Data.description:
Manages the access control for a Linode Database. Only one <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`linode.DatabaseAccessControls`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`linode.DatabaseAccessControls`" pulumi-lang-go="`DatabaseAccessControls`" pulumi-lang-python="`DatabaseAccessControls`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`linode.DatabaseAccessControls`" pulumi-lang-java="`linode.DatabaseAccessControls`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`linode_database_access_controls`">`linode.DatabaseAccessControls`</span> resource should be defined per-database.
For more information, see the Linode APIv4 docs for [MySQL](https://techdocs.akamai.com/linode-api/reference/put-databases-mysql-instance) and [PostgreSQL](https://techdocs.akamai.com/linode-api/reference/put-databases-postgre-sql-instance).

## Example Usage

<!--Start PulumiCodeChooser -->
```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as linode from "@pulumi/linode";

const my_instance = new linode.Instance("my-instance", {
    label: "myinstance",
    region: "us-southeast",
    type: "g6-nanode-1",
    image: "linode/arch",
});
const my_db = new linode.DatabaseMysqlV2("my-db", {
    label: "mydatabase",
    engineId: "mysql/8",
    region: "us-southeast",
    type: "g6-nanode-1",
});
const my_access = new linode.DatabaseAccessControls("my-access", {
    databaseId: my_db.id.apply(x =>Number(x)),
    databaseType: "mysql",
    allowLists: [my_instance.ipAddress],
});
```
```python
import pulumi
import pulumi_linode as linode

my_instance = linode.Instance("my-instance",
    label="myinstance",
    region="us-southeast",
    type="g6-nanode-1",
    image="linode/arch")
my_db = linode.DatabaseMysqlV2("my-db",
    label="mydatabase",
    engine_id="mysql/8",
    region="us-southeast",
    type="g6-nanode-1")
my_access = linode.DatabaseAccessControls("my-access",
    database_id=my_db.id.apply(lambda x: int(x)),
    database_type="mysql",
    allow_lists=[my_instance.ip_address])
```
